&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt&quot;&gt;The first-floor
rear extension, by reason of its excessive bulking and massing, would not
appear subservient to the main dwellinghouse but would appear an overly
dominant addition in relation to the size of the modest mid-terrace dwelling.
Furthermore, its flat roof design would present a discordant feature that does
not reflect the pitched roof design of the host dwelling and terrace row.
&amp;nbsp;As such, the proposed development is contrary to: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;

